---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How to Practice — GlideUp.net"
  description="The different ways to practice on GlideUp — full sessions, exam simulations, domain focus, and how the streak system works."
  activeNav="how-to-use"
>
  <Breadcrumb crumbs={[
    { label: 'Practice', href: '/' },
    { label: 'How to Practice' },
  ]} />

  <h1 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:8px;">How to Practice</h1>
  <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:28px;max-width:680px;line-height:1.6;">
    GlideUp has a few different practice modes depending on how you want to study. Here's what each one does and when to use it.
  </p>

  <div class="mode-grid">

    <article class="card mode-card">
      <div class="mode-card__icon">♾️</div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="mode-card__title">Full Practice</h2>
        <p class="mode-card__desc">
          All questions for the exam, no session limit. The engine prioritizes questions you
          haven't seen yet, followed by questions you've previously gotten wrong. Questions you
          know cold get deprioritized over time. Good for ongoing review and building a complete picture of the exam.
        </p>
        <div class="mode-card__how">Start from the exam dashboard → <strong>Start — 240 questions</strong></div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="card mode-card">
      <div class="mode-card__icon">🎯</div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="mode-card__title">Exam Simulation (Sets 1–4)</h2>
        <p class="mode-card__desc">
          Four distinct 60-question sets per exam, each blueprint-weighted to match the real
          exam's domain distribution. Questions are randomly shuffled every session so the order
          is never the same twice. The four sets are partitioned — running all four covers the
          full bank without exact repeats across sets. Closest thing to sitting the real exam.
        </p>
        <div class="mode-card__how">Exam dashboard → <strong>Modes tab</strong> → pick Exam Sim 1, 2, 3, or 4</div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="card mode-card">
      <div class="mode-card__icon">🔬</div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="mode-card__title">Domain Focus</h2>
        <p class="mode-card__desc">
          Drill a single domain with up to 60 questions. Good if you already know your weak spots
          and want to go deep on one area without cycling through everything else. Each domain card
          shows how many questions are currently available. A second 60Q session unlocks
          automatically once the domain bank reaches 120 questions.
        </p>
        <div class="mode-card__how">Exam dashboard → <strong>Modes tab</strong> → scroll to Domain Focus → pick a domain</div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="card mode-card">
      <div class="mode-card__icon">🧌</div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="mode-card__title">Streak System</h2>
        <p class="mode-card__desc">
          Answer questions in a row without breaking — the feedback escalates as your streak
          builds. First few correct answers are neutral. Hit three in a row and the goblin starts
          paying attention. Five straight and it gets excited. Ten straight and things get a
          little unhinged. Wrong answers reset the streak counter but not your session score.
          The goblin also makes an appearance in the corner every few correct answers.
        </p>
        <div class="mode-card__how">Just answer questions — the streak tracks automatically</div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="card mode-card">
      <div class="mode-card__icon">📊</div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="mode-card__title">Domain Mastery</h2>
        <p class="mode-card__desc">
          Each domain tracks your progress independently. Answer enough questions with high
          accuracy and a domain levels up from Bronze to Silver to Gold. All domains are
          unlocked from question one — there's no gate. The tier reflects how well you know
          the material, not whether you're allowed to practice it.
        </p>
        <div class="mode-card__how">Visible on each exam's Overview tab</div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="card mode-card">
      <div class="mode-card__icon">🔒</div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="mode-card__title">Your Progress is Private</h2>
        <p class="mode-card__desc">
          All progress — XP, streak, domain accuracy, question history — lives in your browser's
          localStorage only. Nothing is sent to a server. No account required. Clearing your
          browser data or switching devices starts fresh. You can reset manually anytime from
          the About page.
        </p>
        <div class="mode-card__how">Reset anytime → <a href="/about/">About</a> → Reset local progress</div>
      </div>
    </article>

  </div>

  <h2 style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin:32px 0 12px;">When to use what</h2>
  <div class="card" style="max-width:680px;">
    <table class="when-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Situation</th><th>Mode</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Just starting a new exam</td><td>Full Practice</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Exam is two weeks away</td><td>Exam Sim sets, rotate through all four</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Exam is tomorrow</td><td>Exam Sim + Domain Focus on weak areas</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Know you're weak on one domain</td><td>Domain Focus</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Want to measure readiness</td><td>Exam Sim — your score at 60Q is a proxy for exam day</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Ongoing maintenance / staying sharp</td><td>Full Practice, a few questions daily</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .mode-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .mode-card { display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: flex-start; }
  .mode-card__icon { font-size: 24px; line-height: 1; margin-top: 2px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .mode-card__title { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 6px; color: var(--text); }
  .mode-card__desc { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .mode-card__how {
    font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted);
    background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px 10px;
  }
  .mode-card__how strong { color: var(--text); }
  .when-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; }
  .when-table th { text-align: left; font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 0 12px 8px 0; }
  .when-table td { padding: 8px 12px 8px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--text-muted); vertical-align: top; }
  .when-table td:last-child { color: var(--primary-dark); font-weight: 500; }
</style>
